<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15295" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">effūsĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		effundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pouring out</i>, <i>pouring
			forth</i>, <i>shedding</i> (a Ciceron. word).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atramenti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 49, 127</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae liquor et effusio, i. e. its property of
					pouring forth,</span>”
				<i>fluidity</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 10, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Judic. 9, 24</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. Gord. Tert. 28, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A pouring</i> or <i>rushing out</i>
			of people: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">effusiones hominum ex oppidis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 22, 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Profusion</i>, <i>prodigality</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Part. 23, 81</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 7,
				3, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 44, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vop. Flor. 1</span></i>.—In the
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecuniarum effusiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 2, 16, 56</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rosc. Am. 46,
			134</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>extravagance</i>,
				<i>excess</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animi in laetitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 31, 66</span></i>
			.</div>
